}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Canvas: notices, empty states and pins","spec":{"accessibility":["Every notice and state is text with an icon, never color alone; the mapping notice is a status region, and a canvas announcement says when a Widget is under a translucent layer.","Pins are focusable buttons named by their thread; an edge indicator or a count is a button named by the side or the number of threads and opens the thread or a list of them with Enter."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (ContextBar, ContextChip, Badge, Button, Alert, EmptyState, Disclosure, Skeleton, Pin, Stack, Text, CanvasStage, SegmentedControl, Segment); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","The edge indicators and the count of a pin cluster are Badge pills, because the Adapter has no pin-count or edge Widget: the real cluster is a teardrop pin carrying the count. The notice chips are outlined Badges at the top left of the frame; the real chips hug the highlight.","The skeleton and the empty states fill the area under the bar and replace the CanvasStage Widget, which cannot be hidden by a Variant, so the stage is wrapped in a Stack that a Variant hides.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (diagnostic codes and paths, Variant names, counts and the MCP tool name); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A View page is open on the canvas. The base state is a live frame with two pins, the Select tool and the zoom controls; Variants add a notice, a chip or a tray button, or replace the frame with a state.","The base zoom is Fit at 93%; while there is no frame to scale, the session chip is drawn no more and every zoom control is disabled.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; with no View selected the render-context controls give way to the canvas title."],"intent":"Show what the canvas says besides the rendered View: the notice when the Workbench cannot measure the Preview, the chips that qualify a highlight, the pins and what stands for pins that cannot be drawn, and the states that replace the frame (an invalid Adapter set, a Variant that cannot run, no View, no Views, loading).","interactionRules":["When the Workbench cannot reliably measure how the Preview is rendered it draws no highlight, outline or pin and says so in one warning above the frame; the structural selection is kept and the notice goes with the condition.","A highlight that cannot be drawn precisely says so in a chip, and a Widget under a translucent layer says that in a chip; both describe only the Preview as it is now, and translucent coverage never hides a pin.","A pin whose Widget is outside the visible canvas is replaced by an edge indicator on that side with the number of threads, and pins close together merge into one count that recomputes from their current positions; threads that cannot be placed, and those beyond what the canvas tracks at once, are counted in the tray at the bottom left.","An invalid Adapter set replaces the frame with a state that says the Widget tree and the Spec stay available, offers Open Adapters and keeps the diagnostics one click away under Details.","A Variant the View no longer defines cannot run, even partially: the canvas says so, names it, and offers Switch to base state as the one primary action and Open in Checks.","With no View selected, or no Views in the Workspace, the canvas says which, and for none names the MCP tool that creates one; while the View is loading it shows a skeleton of the frame."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"}],"requirements":[]},"variants":{"adapter-invalid":{"requirements":["01a115cd-ae9a-7bf9-bd40-8da4bcd669c1"],"state":{"empty-adapter-invalid":{"visible":true},"session-live":{"visible":false},"stage-wrap":{"visible":false},"zoom-fit":{"disabled":true},"zoom-in":{"disabled":true},"zoom-level":{"disabled":true},"zoom-out":{"disabled":true}}},"adapter-invalid-details":{"state":{"adapter-invalid-details":{"open":true},"empty-adapter-invalid":{"visible":true},"session-live":{"visible":false},"stage-wrap":{"visible":false},"zoom-fit":{"disabled":true},"zoom-in":{"disabled":true},"zoom-level":{"disabled":true},"zoom-out":{"disabled":true}}},"loading":{"state":{"bar-chips":{"visible":false},"bar-title":{"visible":true},"empty-loading":{"visible":true},"session-live":{"visible":false},"stage-wrap":{"visible":false},"zoom-fit":{"disabled":true},"zoom-in":{"disabled":true},"zoom-level":{"disabled":true},"zoom-out":{"disabled":true}}},"mapping-paused":{"requirements":["01a11658-2426-777f-8c5f-1b9185054975"],"state":{"mapping-paused":{"visible":true},"pin-js":{"visible":false},"pin-ml":{"visible":false}}},"no-selection":{"state":{"bar-chips":{"visible":false},"bar-title":{"visible":true},"empty-no-selection":{"visible":true},"session-live":{"visible":false},"stage-wrap":{"visible":false},"zoom-fit":{"disabled":true},"zoom-in":{"disabled":true},"zoom-level":{"disabled":true},"zoom-out":{"disabled":true}}},"no-views":{"state":{"bar-chips":{"visible":false},"bar-title":{"visible":true},"empty-no-views":{"visible":true},"session-live":{"visible":false},"stage-wrap":{"visible":false},"zoom-fit":{"disabled":true},"zoom-in":{"disabled":true},"zoom-level":{"disabled":true},"zoom-out":{"disabled":true}}},"pin-cluster":{"requirements":["01a11658-27ae-7f31-ac4f-8e5c0d8d7812"],"state":{"pin-cluster":{"visible":true},"pin-js":{"visible":false},"pin-ml":{"visible":false}}},"pin-edges":{"requirements":["01a11658-276a-7756-ac0e-1f1e00515e27"],"state":{"edge-layer":{"visible":true},"pin-js":{"visible":false},"pin-ml":{"visible":false}}},"precision-unavailable":{"requirements":["01a11687-2d04-704b-88